- Ultraleap Unity Plugin (https://github.com/ultraleap/UnityPlugin), Apache License 2.0, Copyright Ultraleap
  Ltd. No code is copied. The grab thresholds in public/js/interact/config.js are its shipped defaults, read
  from PinchDetector.cs (activateDistance 25 mm, deactivateDistance 30 mm) and GrabHelperObject.cs
  (THOWN_GRAB_COOLDOWNTIME 0.5 s, VELOCITY_HISTORY_LENGTH 45 ms, MAX_VELOCITY_SQUARED 100, and the 0.85
  stickiness factor on a finger that is already pinching). Apache-2.0 is GPL-3.0 compatible.

- The 1 Euro filter in public/js/interact/math.js implements Casiez, Roussel and Vogel, "1 Euro Filter: A
  Simple Speed-based Low-pass Filter for Noisy Input in Interactive Systems", CHI 2012, from the paper. The
  speedFloor term is ours, not theirs.

- The anchor in public/js/interact/grab.js follows the idea in Hilliges, Kim, Izadi, Weiss and Wilson,
  "HoloDesk: Direct 3D Interactions with a Situated See-Through Display", CHI 2012 — a kinematic proxy the
  tracker drives and a dynamic body springed to it — reduced to fingertip proxies, which that paper's
  Limitations section explicitly sanctions where only sparse tracking is available. No code was available to
  copy; there is no open implementation.
